{
  "title": "CoNextions TR® Tendon Repair System",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423255/conextions-tr-r--tendon-repair-system",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Apr 7 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The CoNextions TR® Tendon Repair System is designed for the repair of severed or lacerated tendons",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Novel stainless steel and ultra high tenacity polyethylene implant ensures a strong and flexible repair",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423255/images/6fa8b411-6b6b-413a-86e5-6ba0d19083b8_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_2.44.58_pm.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Implant is designed for the repair of tendons 1.5 - 4.0mm in thickness and 3.0 mm to 9.0 in width",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The CoNextions TR Implant is designed to fit anatomically in intra- and extra- synovial tendons",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Pioneering implant allows surgeons to consistently produce tendon repairs that outperform suture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "2 times stronger repairs than suture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "3.1 times faster repairs than suture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "2.2 times smoother tendon gliding than suture repair",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "CoNextions TR Tendon Repair System is indicated for the repair of severed or lacerated tendons in adults (22 years of age or older)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The product is intended for the following indications:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Digital Flexor Tendons",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Digital Extensor Tendons Proximal to the metacarpophalangeal joints (Zones 6-8)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approach",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Approach the lacerated tendon using a preferred surgical technique",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Create an access point in the sheath by creating a two-centimeter incision over the laceration",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Receive tendon ends using a standard technique and approximate the ends using two epitendineous corner sutures or a preferred alternative approximation technique",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical Specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Comprised of 316 LS stainless steel and Ultra High Molecular Weight Polyethylene (UHMWPE) fiber",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed for tendons at 3 to 9 mm in width and 1.5 to 4 mm in thickness and requires at least 20 mm of surgical site access",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "When deployed, the CoNextions TR Implant is 18 mm in length and 2.8 mm wide",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Assess injured tendon",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "1.5 to 4.0 mm in thickness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "At least 3.0 to 9.0 mm in width",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "20 mm of access (10 mm on either side of injury)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prepare injured tendon",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Approximate tendon ends by placing epitendinous suture loops across the severed tendon",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Place implant mechanism at repair site",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423255/images/0275e629-e22d-43a4-a57c-73a918335193_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_2.42.51_pm.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Insert the tendon cradle under the tendon and position the tendon repair site in the center of the cradle in both the lateral and anterior/posterior plane",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Advance the cartridge by turning the thumb wheel clockwise. Optimal tendon compression is indicated by an audible clicking sound.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Observe the front and back of the tendon through viewing window to ensure proper positioning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Turn thumb wheel counter clockwise to retract cartridge and adjust tendon position as needed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pull back on spring",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Slide top of the implant mechanism to the tip of the deployment mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Connect deployment mechanism to implant mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Caution: Do not rotate deployment mechanism once it is attached to the implant mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Deploy implant",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423255/images/4262a8b3-9dc1-4ae6-87f5-d4e278e8b47c_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_2.42.58_pm.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Fully pull the Deployment Mechanism lever to deploy the implant.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Complete deployment is confirmed when the lever of Deployment Mechanism automatically releases to original position",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Remove retention wire and implant mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Remove retention wire from Tendon Cradle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Turn Thumb Wheel counter clockwise to remove Tendon Cradle from the repair site",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Final repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423255/images/57fc43ba-86c9-46ab-ada7-ae00084a0259_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_2.43.03_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
